{
    /* Diffusion on a ring: a heat step with a periodic boundary, repeated to
       a fixed point. `1 ⌽ U` is the next cell along the axis and `-1 ⌽ U`
       the previous one, wrapping at the ends where `▷` and `▽` would pad
       with zero. The ring relaxes to its mean — slowly: the slowest mode of
       a ring of 256 loses a quarter of a percent a sweep, so a tolerance of
       1e-9 takes a few thousand sweeps, and the kernel says whether it got
       there (rho_kernel_converged) or ran into the cap.

         rhoc examples/periodic.rho --tau 1e-9 --max-iter 20000
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 256 1
    INPUT → U

    (U + (0.25 × (((1 ⌽ U) + (-1 ⌽ U)) - (2.0 × U)))) ⇒ U

    U → =
}
